# Variant of input.lm.ap_htpb_packed_elastic that replaces the Miller-packed
# XYZR sphere IC with a real AP/HTPB backscatter-micrograph IC
# (AP-HTPB-Experimental-Image-Raw.png, the raw grayscale micrograph -- no
# preprocessing script needed). IC::PNG is 2D-only (see src/IC/PNG.H), so
# this file only runs in 2D:
#   mpirun -np 8 ./bin/lowmach-2d-clang++ input.lm.ap_htpb_packed_elastic_png
#
# REWRITE (2026-08-06): this file previously hand-built two pre-blurred,
# pre-padded, pre-complemented PNG images and fed them through a minimal
# local IC::PNG (added this session, supporting only a "value" scale key) --
# multiple iterations of that approach diverged or regressed (see git
# history / session notes around this date for the full trail: an
# immediately-diverging fine mesh, a domain/mesh mismatch against the
# sphere-packed file, and a same-image extra-blur attempt that made things
# worse). That local IC::PNG turned out to predate a much more capable
# GPU-safe IC::PNG/Util::PNG (src/IC/PNG.H, src/Util/PNG.H) already built,
# proven, and run to 57% completion on the eulerian-solids branch (commit
# a858880ba "make PNG gpu safe", see output.lm.ap_htpb_cyclone's
# metadata/diff.patch) -- ported onto this branch wholesale instead of
# continuing to re-derive the same functionality. Its key capabilities used
# below:
#  - threshold: binarizes the sampled channel to a sharp 0/1 indicator
#    before use, instead of treating raw grayscale as a continuous density
#    fraction. The diffuse interface is then built by
#    amr.reinitialize_condensed_composition (already enabled below,
#    inherited from the sphere-packed file) at a controlled width, NOT by
#    manually pre-blurring the source image -- this is what the previous
#    from-scratch attempts got wrong.
#  - invert: lets AP_solid and HTPB_solid read the SAME source image
#    (invert=0 / invert=1), guaranteeing an exact volume-fraction complement
#    by construction. No more separately-generated, separately-blurred
#    AP-IC.png/HTPB-IC.png pair to keep in sync.
#  - plane.normal/plane.point/plane.eps: built-in plane clipping, exactly
#    like PSRead's (see input.lm.ap_htpb_packed_elastic), used below to
#    confine the image to the solid (y<0) region. No more baking a black
#    margin into the image to fake this.
#  - coord.hi must be > coord.lo in each direction now (rotation/flip.x/
#    flip.y control orientation explicitly instead) -- the old "coord.lo
#    maps to the image's first row, not necessarily the smaller y value"
#    footgun documented in earlier versions of this file no longer applies.
#
# Domain/mesh sizing has been revised twice since this file was first
# ported (zoomed out, then zoomed back in slightly + finer dx) -- see the
# amr.n_cell/geometry.prob_lo comments below for the current, authoritative
# values; solid = y<0, gas = y>0 throughout. Elastic-solver conditioning
# rationale (void modulus, max_coarsening_level, etc.) is inherited
# unchanged from input.lm.ap_htpb_packed_elastic -- see that file's header.
#
# Everything else (chemistry, elastic solver settings/conditioning
# workarounds, BCs) is unchanged from input.lm.ap_htpb_packed_elastic -- diff
# against that file, and see its header comments, for the full rationale.

# Required for elastic.solver.abort_on_fail=0 (below) to actually work.
# amrex::Initialize() reads amrex.signal_handling/amrex.throw_exception itself
# ONCE at program startup (ext/AMReX-Codes/amrex/Src/Base/AMReX.cpp) and
# installs its signal handler right then. Solver::Nonlocal::Linear::Parse()
# also injects these same two keys via ParmParse when abort_on_fail=0/
# dump_on_fail=1 is set, but that Parse() call happens much later (when the
# elastic solver object is built, mid-program) -- long after AMReX's signal
# handler is already latched in, so that injection is a no-op in practice.
# Setting them here at top level ensures they're seen at startup instead, so
# MLMG's internal Abort() actually throws a catchable C++ exception (which
# Linear::solve()'s try/catch can then suppress) instead of raising SIGABRT.
amrex.signal_handling = 0
amrex.throw_exception = 1

plot_file = output.lm.ap_htpb_packed_elastic_png
amr.plot_dt = 2.0e-4_s
#amr.plot_int=100
amr.max_level = 0
# ZOOMED-IN-SLIGHTLY, FINER MESH (2026-08-06): x narrowed from the previous
# zoomed-out 2mm to 1.6mm, dx=dy dropped from 3.125um to 2.5um. A stall was
# traced to a real AP/HTPB grain boundary running nearly parallel to the y=0
# solid/gas surface at some x (row 0 of the source image, which IC::PNG
# samples for y=0 and clamps to for all y>0 -- see src/Util/PNG.H's ximg(1)
# clamp -- had a 16-column-wide run of near-threshold pixels there), so the
# material's own diffuse band and the y=0 plane.eps taper (see below) were
# compounding into a stiff, fast-changing composition right at the burning
# surface. Widening plane.eps to compensate was TRIED AND REVERTED (made it
# worse -- see the plane.eps comment further down); the actual fix was
# cropping the source image so a cleaner row lands at y=0 (also further
# down). Finer dx here still helps independently (more cells resolve
# whatever diffuse width the (now cleaner) IC produces).
# n_cell = 640 320 (NOT 640 300 -- first attempt at this used 300, which
# regressed HARD, failing by step 30 instead of ~660: MLMG reported only 3
# MG levels instead of the previous config's 4, because 300 = 2^2*75 only
# halves cleanly twice before hitting an odd factor, starving
# elastic/projection/diffusion.max_coarsening_level=3's assumed coarsening
# depth. 320 = 2^6*5 halves six times -- restores (and exceeds) the original
# mesh's MG depth. Solid/gas split adjusted to 213/107 cells (532.5/267.5um)
# to keep the ~2:1 ratio at this cell count; y domain is now 800um total.
# x HALVED (2026-08-06, later same day, after the crop fix was verified
# stable to step 2000+/t~2.25ms): domain narrowed 1.6mm -> 0.8mm to cut
# compute cost, at the SAME dx=2.5um, so n_cell.x drops 640 -> 320. This is a
# true crop (the source image's x-extent was cropped to its center 432 of
# 864 columns, AP-HTPB-Experimental-Image-Raw-Cropped.png), not a re-stretch
# -- the x pixel scale (1.852um/px) and blur sigma are UNCHANGED, only less
# of the domain (and less of the image) is simulated. y is unchanged (320
# cells, 800um, see below).
amr.n_cell = 320 320
# max_grid_size changed 20 -> 16 (2026-08-06, later same day): 20=2^2*5 only
# halves cleanly twice (20->10->5) before going fractional, one short of
# elastic/projection/diffusion.max_coarsening_level=3's assumed 3 halvings;
# a run at n_cell=640x320 with max_grid_size=20 hit a hard SIGBUS inside
# MLMG's very first V-cycle at STEP 1 (before any residual was even
# printed) -- a memory fault, not a numerical divergence, consistent with a
# box-coarsening edge case. 16=2^4 halves cleanly 4 times; both n_cell
# values (320, 320) are still evenly divisible by it (20, 20 boxes).
amr.max_grid_size = 16
amr.blocking_factor = 2
amr.regrid_int = 5
amr.grid_eff = 0.7
amr.nsubsteps = 1
amr.reinitialize_condensed_composition = 1
amr.reinitialize_condensed_composition_eta_min = 0.99
# Elastic fields (disp/stress/strain) are nodal; mirror them into the *cell*
# plotfiles too so they can be sampled the same way as the scalar fields.
amr.cell.all = 1
amr.node.any = 0

# Inert with amr.max_level = 0 above (see input.lm.ap_htpb_packed_elastic's
# WARNING) -- left in place in case AMR is ever restorable here.
eta_refinement_criterion = 0.5
temperature_refinement_criterion = 1.0
velocity_refinement_criterion = 1.0

timestep = 1.0e-7_s
stop_time = 100_ms
dynamictimestep.on = 1
dynamictimestep.min = 1.0e-12
dynamictimestep.max = 5.0e-6
dynamictimestep.verbose = 0

integration.type = RungeKutta
integration.rk.type = 3

# dx = dy = 2.5um; x is +-0.4mm (halved, see amr.n_cell comment above), y is
# -0.5325mm (solid) to +0.2675mm (gas), z left at +-0.25mm (unused, 2D-only
# file).
geometry.prob_lo = -0.4_mm -0.5325_mm -0.25_mm
geometry.prob_hi =  0.4_mm  0.2675_mm  0.25_mm
geometry.is_periodic = 0 0 0

# Gas species 0-5 retain the ordering required by the Rocfire mechanism:
# AP, binder, monopropellant, premixed, primary-flame, final-flame products.
system.amount = kmol
gas.mw = 26.0_g/mol 26.0_g/mol 26.0_g/mol 26.0_g/mol 26.0_g/mol 26.0_g/mol
gas.thermo.type = rocfire
gas.thermo.rocfire.mw = 26.0_g/mol
gas.thermo.rocfire.cp_mass = 0.3_cal/g/K
gas.thermo.rocfire.Tref = 273.15_K
gas.transport.type = rocfire
gas.transport.rocfire.mw = 26.0_g/mol
gas.transport.rocfire.prandtl = 0.69
gas.transport.rocfire.lewis = 1.0
gas.transport.rocfire.lambda_a = 2.13037e-7_cal/cm/s/K^2
gas.transport.rocfire.lambda_b = 5.32743e-6_cal/cm/s/K
gas.eos.type = tpg

species.names = AP_gas HTPB_gas Mono Premixed Primary Final AP_solid HTPB_solid
AP_gas.mechanics = fluid
HTPB_gas.mechanics = fluid
Mono.mechanics = fluid
Premixed.mechanics = fluid
Primary.mechanics = fluid
Final.mechanics = fluid
AP_solid.mechanics = rigid_solid
HTPB_solid.mechanics = rigid_solid
AP_solid.reference_density = 1950.0_kg/m^3
HTPB_solid.reference_density = 920.0_kg/m^3
AP_solid.specific_heat = 1297.90_J/kg/K
AP_solid.thermal_conductivity = 0.4186_W/m/K
HTPB_solid.specific_heat = 2418.29_J/kg/K
HTPB_solid.thermal_conductivity = 0.1300_W/m/K

# Elastic constants, converted from representative literature isotropic
# (E, nu) values via mu = E/(2*(1+nu)), kappa = E/(3*(1-2*nu)):
#   AP crystal:    E ~ 21.6 GPa, nu ~ 0.14  -> mu ~ 9.47 GPa,  kappa ~ 10.0 GPa
#   HTPB binder:   E ~ 5.0 MPa,  nu ~ 0.499 (near-incompressible rubber)
#                                            -> mu ~ 1.67 MPa, kappa ~ 833 MPa
# These are representative orders of magnitude for the pure phases, not a fit
# to this specific formulation -- replace with measured/calibrated values if
# available. See input.lm.ap_htpb_packed_elastic's WARNING regarding solver
# conditioning at these magnitudes.
AP_solid.elastic.model.mu    = 9.47e6 # true SI 9.47e9 -- see WARNING above (1e4x rescale)
AP_solid.elastic.model.kappa = 1.00e8 # true SI 1.00e10 -- see WARNING above (1e4x rescale)
HTPB_solid.elastic.model.mu    = 1.67e6 # = true SI value -- see WARNING above (1e4x rescale)
HTPB_solid.elastic.model.kappa = 8.33e8 # = true SI value -- see WARNING above (1e4x rescale)

# Soft void: the gas region gets a small but nonzero modulus (in the same
# units as the solid moduli above, i.e. also 1e4x-rescaled) instead of being
# masked by psi's 1e-8 floor. See input.lm.ap_htpb_packed_elastic's WARNING
# for the full derivation of these contrast ratios.
# DEBUG: void stiffened 10x from the original 5.0e3/4.0e5 (contrast vs.
# AP/HTPB now ~25-189x, below the file's documented [~250,~2100]x
# accuracy-plateau range but still far under the ~30,000x stability limit)
# to test whether reducing solid/void contrast helps the elastic MLMG
# solve, which now diverges catastrophically around step 10-11 (after the
# Final.density.ic/temperature.ic pad-offset vacuum-density fix let the run
# get that far in the first place). Revert to 5.0e3/4.0e5 if this doesn't
# help, since it trades accuracy for stability margin.
elastic.void.model.mu    = 5.0e4
elastic.void.model.kappa = 4.0e6

chemistry.model.type = rocfire
chemistry.model.rocfire.A = 27.0e3_g/cm^3/s 25.3e3_g/cm^3/s 5.0e3_g/cm^3/s 0.4e3_g/cm^3/s
chemistry.model.rocfire.pressure_exponent = 1.6 1.7 1.7 1.7
chemistry.model.rocfire.activation_energy = 15.9_kcal/mol 14.5_kcal/mol 11.3_kcal/mol 14.5_kcal/mol
chemistry.model.rocfire.qgas = 430.0_cal/g 447.0_cal/g 8365.0_cal/g 2127.0_cal/g
chemistry.model.rocfire.qsolid = -100.0_cal/g -300.0_cal/g
chemistry.model.rocfire.pressure_reference = 1.0_bar
# TIGHTENED (2026-08-06): the v7 (x-halved) run never hit a chemistry solver
# failure (Model::Chemistry::Chemistry::Advance already adaptively subcycles
# within each hydro dt, halving/doubling chemistry_dt on Newton
# non-convergence -- see src/Model/Chemistry/Chemistry.H -- and hard-aborts
# with "Local chemistry integration failed" if that subcycling can't
# converge; that message never appeared in the v7 log), but it DID show a
# temperature runaway (2500K real flame temp -> 16000K over ~85 steps,
# starting right where the surface had locally burned through) right before
# the eventual Diffusion.cpp MLMG abort. The old reltol/abstol (1e-8/1e-12)
# let each substep's Newton iteration accept a residual that, integrated
# over many stiff substeps near a burn-through point, could still
# accumulate enough error to overshoot the true adiabatic flame temperature.
# Tightened both tolerances by 2 orders of magnitude and raised max_iter so
# the (still-adaptive) substepping has room to actually reach the tighter
# tolerance instead of prematurely halving chemistry_dt toward the 40-
# rejection abort limit.
chemistry.solver.type = backward_euler
chemistry.solver.backward_euler.max_iter = 300
chemistry.solver.backward_euler.reltol = 1.0e-10
chemistry.solver.backward_euler.abstol = 1.0e-14

# AP uses the 1-6 MPa monopropellant calibration from LMRFMonoAP. HTPB uses the
# approximately 4 mm/s calibration from the 3 MPa sandwich configuration.
# The phase-field gradient terms are integrated implicitly.
mechanisms.names = AP_decomposition HTPB_pyrolysis
AP_decomposition.type = phase_change
AP_decomposition.phase_change.in = AP_solid
AP_decomposition.phase_change.out = AP_gas
AP_decomposition.phase_change.rate_multiplier = 2.75e6
AP_decomposition.phase_change.activation_temperature = 3145.0_K
AP_decomposition.phase_change.temperature_cutoff = 360.0_K
AP_decomposition.phase_change.phase_field.type = allencahn
AP_decomposition.phase_change.phase_field.allencahn.mobility = 0.01_1/Pa/s
AP_decomposition.phase_change.phase_field.allencahn.lambda = 8.333333333333333_Pa
AP_decomposition.phase_change.phase_field.allencahn.kappa = 1.0e-8_J/m
AP_decomposition.phase_change.phase_field.allencahn.w0 = 0.0
AP_decomposition.phase_change.phase_field.allencahn.w12 = 2.0
AP_decomposition.phase_change.phase_field.allencahn.w1 = 1.0

HTPB_pyrolysis.type = phase_change
HTPB_pyrolysis.phase_change.in = HTPB_solid
HTPB_pyrolysis.phase_change.out = HTPB_gas
HTPB_pyrolysis.phase_change.rate_multiplier = 1.85e5
HTPB_pyrolysis.phase_change.activation_temperature = 3145.0_K
HTPB_pyrolysis.phase_change.temperature_cutoff = 360.0_K
HTPB_pyrolysis.phase_change.phase_field.type = allencahn
HTPB_pyrolysis.phase_change.phase_field.allencahn.mobility = 0.01_1/Pa/s
HTPB_pyrolysis.phase_change.phase_field.allencahn.lambda = 8.333333333333333_Pa
HTPB_pyrolysis.phase_change.phase_field.allencahn.kappa = 1.0e-8_J/m
HTPB_pyrolysis.phase_change.phase_field.allencahn.w0 = 0.0
HTPB_pyrolysis.phase_change.phase_field.allencahn.w12 = 2.0
HTPB_pyrolysis.phase_change.phase_field.allencahn.w1 = 1.0

rigid.relaxation_time = 1.0e-8_s
rigid.velocity = 0.0 0.0 0.0

advection.type = muscl
advection.muscl.limiter.type = minmod
cfl = 0.8
phase_field.cfl = 1.5
# NEW (2026-08-06): caps the diffusion number (kappa/(rho*cp)*dt/dx^2) using
# the max thermal conductivity anywhere in the domain, even though
# conduction is solved implicitly here (implicit diffusion is
# unconditionally linearly stable, so src/Integrator/LowMach.cpp normally
# skips this check entirely whenever implicit_thermal_diffusion is set --
# see the conduction_cfl comment in LowMach::Parse). Added specifically to
# bound how fast DT is allowed to stay large while the temperature-runaway
# instability (see the plane.eps comment above) is developing: Rocfire's
# thermal_conductivity = lambda_a*T + lambda_b grows linearly with T, and a
# spiking coefficient combined with a large DT is what appears to destabilize
# the nonlinear diffusion MLMG solve even though the linear operator itself
# is unconditionally stable. Same 0.5 safety factor as the existing
# (explicit-only) viscous/conductive check.
conduction_cfl = 0.5
include_viscosity = 1
implicit_viscosity = 1
include_conduction = 1
advect_temperature = 1
projection.enabled = 1
projection.tol_rel = 1.0e-11
projection.tol_abs = 1.0e-12
projection.verbose = 0
projection.update_pressure = 1
# DEBUG: switched back to hard-abort (was 0). With elastic.interval=1000
# (see below -- confirmed this session as the fix for the elastic-driven
# blowup, verified stable to step 2685+ on input.lm.ap_htpb_packed_elastic),
# this file still diverges: pressure/velocity blow up (checked via yt at
# step 152: pressure ~1.5e15 Pa, velocity ~4e5-8e5 m/s, vs. ~3e6 Pa / ~cm/s
# expected) even though elastic is frozen until step 1000. With
# abort_on_fail=0 this failure was silent -- the run just ground down to
# dynamictimestep.min (1e-12) and stalled with no error. Restored to abort
# so the next run stops exactly where projection/diffusion first stops
# converging, to localize this second, elastic-independent divergence.
projection.abort_on_fail = 1
# Cap MLMG coarsening depth, matching elastic.max_coarsening_level = 3 --
# without this (root cause found by tracing pressure growth: 3e6 -> 2.5e11
# over 21 steps because projection never actually converges), MLMG coarsens
# straight through the diffuse rigid/fluid interface in the mobility-scaled
# beta = mobility/density coefficient field (LowMach.cpp), producing garbage
# coarse operators -- the same failure mode elastic was already protected
# against. Added matching max_coarsening_level ParmParse handling to both
# operators (src/Operator/PressurePoisson.cpp, src/Operator/Diffusion.cpp).
projection.max_coarsening_level = 3
diffusion.tol_rel = 1.0e-11
diffusion.tol_abs = 1.0e-12
diffusion.verbose = 0
diffusion.abort_on_fail = 1
diffusion.max_coarsening_level = 3
#diagnostics.interval = 100
diagnostics.extended_fields = 0

# The common diffuse condensed/gas surface is y=0. Both materials read the
# SAME raw micrograph (AP-HTPB-Experimental-Image-Raw.png, 864x480,
# grayscale so channel choice doesn't matter -- g picked for consistency
# with the working cyclone reference run); invert makes HTPB the exact
# complement of AP. fit=coord stretches the full image onto x in
# [-0.25mm, 0.25mm], y in [-0.25mm, 0.0mm] (the solid bed only). threshold
# binarizes each sample to 0/1 (0.5 in the default 0-255-normalized range,
# landing almost exactly on this image's ~127 mean pixel value); the actual
# diffuse interface comes from amr.reinitialize_condensed_composition below,
# not from the image. plane.normal/point/eps clip the image to y<0 (a soft
# tanh transition over plane.eps, matching PSRead's usage in
# input.lm.ap_htpb_packed_elastic) instead of relying on any padding baked
# into the image -- so, unlike the abandoned padded-image approach, rigid_eta
# is now genuinely 0 for all y>0 with no separate pad-offset bookkeeping
# needed in Final.density.ic/temperature.ic below.
# DIFFUSE INTERFACE (2026-08-06): threshold removed and the source image
# swapped for AP-HTPB-Experimental-Image-Diffuse.png, a pre-processed copy
# (scripts/microstructure_to_diffuse_interface.py) of the raw micrograph:
# binarized at 127.5/255 (matching the old threshold=0.5) then Gaussian-
# blurred with an ANISOTROPIC sigma chosen so the blur is isotropic in
# PHYSICAL space despite the image being stretched non-uniformly onto the
# domain. amr.reinitialize_condensed_composition does NOT create or widen a
# diffuse interface (it only re-snaps species ratios in already-mostly-full
# cells, eta>=eta_min, to avoid corrupting whatever interface already
# exists) -- the diffuse width has to come from the IC itself, so threshold
# is omitted and the continuous (blurred) grayscale value is used directly
# as the volume fraction.
# plane.eps WIDENING REVERTED, IMAGE CROPPED/SHIFTED INSTEAD (2026-08-06,
# later same day): widening plane.eps to 40um (tried first) made things
# WORSE -- it failed by step ~30 (t~5e-5s) instead of step ~660 (t~2ms),
# because the two diffuse fronts (material grain boundary, y=0 plane taper)
# were spatially correlated (a real boundary sits right at the surface at
# some x), so widening the taper just pulled MORE of the grain-boundary band
# into the overlap instead of independently smoothing either one. Reverted
# plane.eps to the original 20um (and Final.density.ic.expression's tanh
# width back to 20.0e-6 to match). Root cause fixed properly instead: the
# raw micrograph is genuinely a poor fit at row 0 (the row IC::PNG samples
# for y=0, and clamps to for the whole y>0 gas region -- see
# src/Util/PNG.H's ximg(1) clamp) -- row 0 has boundaries running nearly
# PARALLEL to the surface at several x (verified: max contiguous run of
# near-threshold pixels = 16/864 columns at row 0, vs. rows found by scanning
# all 480 rows for the smallest such run). AP-HTPB-Experimental-Image-Raw.png
# was cropped starting at row 173 (AP-HTPB-Experimental-Image-Raw-Cropped.png,
# 864x307, discarding the top 173 rows) so the row that now lands at y=0 has
# only a 5-column max parallel run -- much less likely to compound with the
# plane taper. The crop shortens the pixel count over the same 532.5um solid
# depth (864x307 instead of 864x480), so the blur sigma was recomputed for
# the coarser y pixel scale (532.5um/307px=1.735um/px, x unchanged at
# 1.6mm/864px=1.852um/px) keeping the same ~15um/~6-cell target width:
# sigma_x_px=4.56/1.852=2.46 (unchanged), sigma_y_px=4.56/1.735=2.63.
AP_solid.density.ic.type = png
AP_solid.density.ic.png.filename = AP-HTPB-Experimental-Image-Diffuse.png
AP_solid.density.ic.png.channel = g
AP_solid.density.ic.png.fit = coord
AP_solid.density.ic.png.coord.lo = -0.4_mm -0.5325_mm
AP_solid.density.ic.png.coord.hi =  0.4_mm  0.0_mm
AP_solid.density.ic.png.flip.y = 1
AP_solid.density.ic.png.invert = false
# plane.eps set to 0 (2026-08-06, later same day): traced the t~2.37ms
# Diffusion.cpp MLMG crash back to a phantom-fuel bug, not a stiffness/
# tolerance issue (chemistry.solver.backward_euler tolerance tightening by
# 2 orders of magnitude made zero difference -- same crash, same step).
# Root cause: IC::PNG clamps EVERY y>0 (gas-region) sample to row 0 of the
# source image (src/Util/PNG.H's ximg(1) clamp), and this soft tanh
# plane.eps mask never reaches exactly 0 -- at y=56um with eps=20um,
# mask=0.5*(1+tanh(2*(-56)/20))~6e-6, small but nonzero. That let row 0's
# real AP/HTPB texture (nonzero away from a pure-HTPB-or-AP column) bleed,
# attenuated but never eliminated, arbitrarily far up into the gas as trace
# rigid_species_eta/component_density (verified: HTPB_solid density
# ~4e-6 relative at y=56-61um, x~96-99um, exactly where row 0 has an
# AP/HTPB grain boundary). That trace "ghost" HTPB sits in a low-density/
# low-heat-capacity gas cell, ignites once T crosses
# HTPB_pyrolysis.phase_change.temperature_cutoff=360K (quickly, from the
# initial exponential temperature profile), and the resulting small heat
# release produces an outsized local dT -- kicking off the runaway
# (T: 434K at step 401 -> 16000K+ by step 635) that eventually kills the
# diffusion solve. Now that the diffuse interface comes from the
# pre-blurred image (not from plane.eps -- see the DIFFUSE INTERFACE
# comment above), plane.eps's only remaining job is to hard-zero material
# for y>0, so it should be a true hard cutoff (eps=0 -> the
# `distance >= 0.0` branch in IC::PNG::Add, not the tanh branch -- see
# src/IC/PNG.H) instead of a soft taper with a never-quite-zero tail.
AP_solid.density.ic.png.plane.normal = 0.0 -1.0 0.0
AP_solid.density.ic.png.plane.point = 0.0_mm 0.0_mm 0.0_mm
AP_solid.density.ic.png.plane.eps = 0.0_um
AP_solid.density.ic.png.value = 1950.0_kg/m^3

HTPB_solid.density.ic.type = png
HTPB_solid.density.ic.png.filename = AP-HTPB-Experimental-Image-Diffuse.png
HTPB_solid.density.ic.png.channel = g
HTPB_solid.density.ic.png.fit = coord
HTPB_solid.density.ic.png.coord.lo = -0.4_mm -0.5325_mm
HTPB_solid.density.ic.png.coord.hi =  0.4_mm  0.0_mm
